264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 683 0 R
/E (High operating leverage means a company has more fixed costs than variable costs. If the economy is growing, you can assume the company is increasing revenue. With higher percentage of fixed costs, a larger portion of that revenue can be retained as profit. The key point is that variable costs increase with revenue, while fixed costs remain constant.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [13]
>>
